-- title:
--   Injectivity of the idelic lattice dictionary
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated (`hfg`) and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$ (`hspan`), so that $\Lambda$ is a full lattice in a finite-dimensional $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra. Write $\widehat{D} = D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, the base change of $D$ along the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ formed from $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $\widehat{\Lambda} =$ [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) be the additive subgroup of $\widehat{D}$ generated by the elements $z \otimes a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a$ a finite adele all of whose components lie in the corresponding adic completion of the integers. For a unit $g$ of $\widehat{D}$, [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ consisting of those $x \in D$ whose image $x \otimes 1$ under $D \to \widehat{D}$ lies in the left translate $g \cdot \widehat{\Lambda}$, i.e. $D \cap g\widehat{\Lambda}$. The assertion is that for units $g, g'$ of $\widehat{D}$ one has $D \cap g\widehat{\Lambda} = D \cap g'\widehat{\Lambda}$ if and only if $g^{-1}g'$ lies in [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26), the stabiliser of the underlying set of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ under the pointwise multiplication action of the unit group of $\widehat{D}$.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the idelic dictionary for lattices: a translate $g\widehat{\Lambda}$ is determined by its global points, so $g \mapsto D \cap g\widehat{\Lambda}$ induces an injection from $\widehat{D}^{\times}$ modulo the stabiliser of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ into the lattices of $D$ (for $\Lambda$ an order, the stabiliser is $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$). It is used in the comparison of class sets with quotients of the coset graph in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, and in identifying classes of lattices arising from strong approximation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_ofFiniteIdele_eq_ofFiniteIdele_iff.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped TensorProduct Pointwise
open IsDedekindDomain NumberField

theorem Submodule.ofFiniteIdele_eq_ofFiniteIdele_iff
    {D : Type*} [Ring D] [Algebra ℚ D]
    (Λ : Submodule ℤ D) (hfg : Λ.FG) (hspan : Submodule.span ℚ (Λ : Set D) = ⊤)
    (g g' : (D ⊗[ℚ] FiniteAdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ)ˣ) :
    Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ g = Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ g' ↔
      g⁻¹ * g' ∈ Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer Λ := by sorry
